---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/brevo';
const title = 'Brevo for Shopify: PushOwl, imports and message ownership';
const desc = 'Choose the current Brevo Shopify connection, reconcile imported preferences and decide who sends receipts, access emails and marketing.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">← All app reviews</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Shopify operations · checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Brevo for Shopify: PushOwl, imports and message ownership</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Brevo deserves a Shopify evaluation when you want marketing channels and a transactional sending service under one supplier. Start by choosing the right connection and account. A low headline email price does not settle which app owns customer imports, cart reminders, receipts or course access.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Use the current Shopify connection</h2>
      <p>Brevo’s <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360014912879-Brevo-PushOwl-app-for-Shopify-Connect-your-Shopify-store-with-Brevo-PushOwl">Shopify connection guide</a> identifies Brevo PushOwl as the supported connection, replacing the former app for new stores. It documents customer, product, collection and order sync, an onsite tracker, product blocks, and welcome, browse, back-in-stock and cart use cases. This is more capable than the old description of a basic email bridge.</p>
      <p>The same guide describes email, SMS, web push and WhatsApp. Treat each channel as a separate setup and audience decision. A visitor accepting browser push has not thereby subscribed to SMS. Confirm the available destination, sender and plan in your account before making one channel a prerequisite for a flow.</p>
      <p>The practical benefit is keeping store data and messaging work together. For a home-goods shop, product content and browse recovery can be evaluated within this connection before adding another app. For an existing Brevo user, selecting the right account matters as much as selecting a template.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Make the import a controlled data decision</h2>
      <p>The connection guide warns that Shopify becomes the customer-data source of truth on import and may overwrite existing Brevo attributes, including subscription status. Preserve a pre-import export with withdrawals and capture evidence. Compare a small record set before allowing historical data to drive campaigns.</p>
      <p>Build a mapping table with Shopify field, existing Brevo attribute, expected winner and affected workflow. Include a withdrawn contact, a changed email, a customer with no marketing subscription and a profile already present in Brevo. Resolve conflicts before sending; a successful background import is not proof that preferences survived.</p>
      <p>Check the account selected during onboarding against its billing owner, domains, existing lists and API integrations. Accidentally creating a second account can divide campaign history from store data. Record where old suppression evidence and transactional logs will remain accessible, and which account support should investigate if a customer reports a duplicate.</p>
      <p>After import, reconcile source and destination counts with explained exclusions, inspect representative order histories and confirm the tracker in the live theme. Give unresolved records a hold status rather than inventing permission from their presence in Shopify.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Four evaluations with different acceptance evidence</h2>
      <p>These are proposed store exercises, not observed tests, launch times or revenue improvements. Keep screenshots or logs of the expected state and failures so an operator can repeat them after a change.</p>
      <p><strong>German home-goods signup:</strong> preview the actual language and confirmation link, then test unconfirmed, confirmed and withdrawn contacts. Confirm which state enters the welcome flow and what Shopify receives. A German template or double opt-in feature alone does not establish compliance. Keep product recommendations useful even when no purchase history exists.</p>
      <p><strong>€72 cart:</strong> choose reminder timing and a shipping offer from your own margin and customer expectations. Test a returning buyer, an unidentified visitor and an order placed between reminders. Establish which event identifies the cart and which sender cancels the pending job. If email and push both run, record their separate permissions and the intended order of touches.</p>
      <p><strong>Digital course purchase:</strong> enumerate the Shopify order confirmation, payment receipt, access link, password reset and optional promotional onboarding. Give each exactly one sending owner. Place a test purchase and resend the access link without sending a duplicate receipt or enrolling an ineligible buyer in marketing. An access failure belongs in a support queue even when a campaign dashboard looks healthy.</p>
      <p><strong>Apparel basics reorder:</strong> use the original 60-day consumption assumption as a hypothesis, not a measured cycle. Check size and SKU mapping, refunded orders and intervening purchases before a reminder near day 55. Preview a discontinued item and a buyer whose product was a gift. Measure repeat contribution separately from reminder clicks; no 6.1% reorder result or threefold setup penalty has been established.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Transactional capability does not transfer Shopify ownership</h2>
      <p>Brevo offers transactional sending; its <a class="link" href="https://help.brevo.com/hc/en-us/articles/7924148470546-How-can-I-send-transactional-emails-with-Brevo">transactional email guide</a> describes available sending approaches. Confirm the supported method for each application. Installing a marketing connection is not acceptance evidence that Shopify’s native order notifications have been replaced or disabled.</p>
      <p>For a digital-product store, write a dispatch ledger: triggering system, template, recipient, provider, retry identifier and support owner. Have the application prevent duplicate access grants when a request is retried. Distinguish provider acceptance from delivery and from successful course access. Handle bounces and expired access links with a recovery path that staff can use.</p>
      <p>Authenticate the actual sending domains and inventory DNS ownership before moving traffic. Separate marketing and service templates and monitoring where useful, but do not promise subdomains isolate reputation or improve delivery. Keep essential service messages narrowly tied to their purpose; permission for an order receipt does not authorize a promotional upsell sequence.</p>
      <p>A unified supplier can reduce billing and support handoffs if it serves these jobs well. A split stack can also be sensible if an existing access service is reliable. Compare incident handling, resend controls and logs before replacing it merely to reduce the number of vendor names.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Quote the app and the sending workload together</h2>
      <p>Use the pricing link in the Shopify connection guide for <a class="link" href="https://pushowl.com/pricing">Brevo PushOwl plans</a>, and check <a class="link" href="https://www.brevo.com/pricing/">Brevo pricing</a> for the other products you need. Ask which subscription covers the app, transactional traffic and each channel; do not assume a standalone marketing plan covers everything. No universal $35–55 monthly bill is established here.</p>
      <p><strong>Home goods:</strong> 6,000 emails and 2,000 SMS per month need recipient destinations, message segments and the split between campaigns and automations. Add capture and any push workload before requesting the quote. Compare identical volumes against alternatives rather than assigning Klaviyo an invented equivalent price.</p>
      <p><strong>Apparel:</strong> 45,000 monthly emails is a workload, not evidence that 380 orders requires a particular supplier. Reserve flow volume before scheduling campaigns, and quote an ordinary month and a seasonal peak. Record taxes, paid features and operating time separately from message spend.</p>
      <p><strong>Digital products:</strong> 120,000 marketing emails plus 30,000 transactional emails totals 150,000 messages. Keep both categories explicit when confirming allowances and billing. Include retries and access resends in the forecast where billable, and compare the unified quote with the actual replacement invoices rather than assuming $140–200 or guaranteed savings.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Choose on maintained operations, not migration stories</h2>
      <p>Retain Brevo on the shortlist when the PushOwl data path, required channels and service-message handling meet the acceptance cases above at an acceptable total cost. Product blocks, behavioral journeys and the transactional service are real reasons to evaluate it; predictive segmentation or a specific reporting requirement should be demonstrated against your own data.</p>
      <p>If weekly tag exports are necessary, document the missing field and its business consequence first. Check whether configuration or a supported integration solves it before migrating. Compare a sample workflow and a contribution report in the destination. No two-warning rule, six-hour threshold or mandatory move to Sequenzy follows from manual work.</p>
      <p>There are no observed home-goods wins or apparel migrations behind this review. Keep one owner for imports, one for storefront tracking and one for service delivery, even if one person fills all three roles. That makes an account or theme change reviewable without treating cheap sending as automatic retention strategy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8"><h2>Continue the evaluation</h2><ul>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo profile and event operations</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend capture and channel ownership</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy API and event maintenance</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">Messaging pricing guide</a></li>
    </ul></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
